Solution

Expected Outcome: Pipeline accepts params, runs parallels conditionally, times out on errors, requires approval.
Enhanced Jenkinsfile:groovypipeline {
    agent any
    parameters {
        string(name: 'BRANCH_TO_BUILD', defaultValue: 'main', description: 'Branch to build')
    }
    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                git branch: "${params.BRANCH_TO_BUILD}", url: 'https://github.com/<user>/repo.git'
            }
        }
        stage('Parallel Tests') {
            parallel {
                stage('Unit') { steps { sh 'mvn test -Dtest=Unit*' } }
                stage('Integration') { steps { sh 'mvn test -Dtest=Integration*' } }
            }
        }
        stage('Approval') {
            steps {
                input message: 'Deploy to staging?', ok: 'Yes'
            }
        }
        stage('Deploy') {
            steps {
                timeout(time: 5, unit: 'MINUTES') {
                    sh 'echo "Deploying..."'
                }
            }
        }
    }
    post {
        always {
            script {
                try {
                    emailext subject: "Build ${currentBuild.result}", to: 'team@example.com'
                } catch (e) {
                    echo "Email failed: ${e}"
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
Verification: Trigger with param 'dev' > Observe parallel execution in Blue Ocean; approve stage pauses. Abort test: Pipeline marks unstable.
Production Guideline: Use currentBuild.result for status; integrate with GitHub Checks API for PR status.
